  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe standard seems to be unclear about whether `valueAsNumber` for `<input type=time>` and `<input type=datetime-local>` should be rounded or floored: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#time-state-(type=time):concept-input-value-number-string (perhaps the core of the issue here is that there is no unambiguous mapping from *time* to *valid time string*)\ne.g. if you set `valueAsNumber = 59999.6` for `type=time`, should the value be set to `00:00:59.999` or `00:01`?\nCurrently there is inconsistency across browsers: Chromium rounds datetime but floors time, whereas Firefox floors both.\nI realize that this is a very minute issue, but maybe it is still worth clarifying 🙂 \n",
